  "original_scope": "Parent #6175, foundation #5113 (closed). Related #6181 (larger compositor service domain), #6180 (timing). \n## Problem\nx86_64 `arch/x86_64/domain_transition.rs` switches CR3 on entry/return; protection costs, TLB effects, shared-window copies, register/interrupt preservation and service launch cost are not independently attributed for repeated ordinary services.\n## Outcome\nPublish source-pinned exact no-op and payload sweep measurements for CPL3 entry/exit, trap, page-table switch, memory copies, hot/warm domain return and staged IPC. Only optimize a demonstrated hot cost while retaining isolation, capability checks and correct faults.\n## Work\n- Benchmark 0/short/bounded-large requests, reused vs fresh domain, nested timer preemption and fault paths; distinguish raw TSC from calibrated time.\n- Evaluate stable mappings and PCID tagging where CPU feature and correct invalidation/ASID lifetime make it safe; unsupported CPUs retain conservative path.\n- Verify flush/revocation on domain restart or reused PCID, no stale sibling/Root mappings, no FPU or interrupt-state leakage; compare kernel timing and total responsive-journey wall clock.\n## Acceptance\nReproducible baseline and before/after evidence with exact source/CPU/QEMU, semantic/protection equivalence and negative isolation tests. No speculative PCID deployment, no weakening page/I/O privilege, no source-level concurrency/scheduler redefinition.",
